@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}
<section class="page-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">DATA HANDLING</p>
    <h1>Privacy and security</h1>
    <p>SafeVault stores note titles and contents in a local SQLite database for this learning project. Access is restricted to the signed-in owner.</p>
</section>
<div class="panel">
    <h2>Security controls in this sample</h2>
    <ul class="check-list">
        <li>Passwords are handled by ASP.NET Identity's password hasher, not stored as plaintext.</li>
        <li>Cookie-authenticated POST forms use anti-forgery validation.</li>
        <li>Razor's normal text rendering encodes user content; the application does not use <code>Html.Raw</code> for notes.</li>
        <li>API requests use short-lived signed JWTs with issuer, audience, signature, and lifetime validation.</li>
        <li>Secrets should be supplied through environment variables or user-secrets, never committed to Git.</li>
    </ul>
</div>
